johnny knoxville is one of america's  most recognizable daredevils but which  stunt forced him to use a catheter for  three years you might not want to know  the answer and more things you might not  know about the jackass forever star just  ahead johnny knoxville born philip john  clapp is no stranger to injuries in  hospital visits but he also  unfortunately had many medical issues as  a child in an interview with rolling  stone he details the asthma issues he  had as a kid and which he still deals  with today he told the magazine it was a  really nice childhood and i was really  cuddled but i was also sick a lot his  asthma was so bad that he couldn't do a  lot of classic childhood activities like  playing in a pile of leaves knoxville  even had stints in which he had to spend  several days to a week in the hospital  he said he almost died at the age of  eight as a result of having the flu  pneumonia and bronchitis all at the same  time yet his chronic lung disease didn't  stop him from playing sports because he  quote didn't want to be left out or feel  like a victim johnny knoxville is  technically a classically trained actor  even though his training was never  formally completed according to the new  york times knoxville moved to los  angeles after high school and attended  the pasadena school of dramatic arts but  he dropped out after six weeks knoxville  told the washington times that he had  wanted to be an actor since he was 13  because it sounded like a job with the  least amount of work involved as luck  would have it knoxville would eventually  make it in the acting world without a  fancy degree yet it took some time and a  unique career path before he made his  way to stardom before jackass was born  knoxville was a writer for skateboarding  magazine big brother where he pitched  the story about testing self-defense  equipment like pepper spray and stun  guns on himself magazine editor jeff  tremaine suggested knoxville film the  experiments and the rest as they say is  history  knoxville's inaugural acting credit was  an appearance on the ben stiller show in  1992 it wasn't a major role as knoxville  was a featured extra as a cure fan other  roles audiences might have missed  knoxville and include a college guy and  coyote ugly in 2002 as well as bob and  desert blues in 1995. though he had  already made a name for himself by the  time he took the part audiences might be  surprised to learn that he voiced johnny  krill on spongebob squarepants but while  knoxville has played a plethora of roles  outside of the jackass franchise most  people would agree that his greatest  performances happen when he's just being  himself knoxville is widely known as a  stunt performer and actor but fans might  not know that he also has numerous  writing credits knoxville has 15 writing  credits on imdb including projects such  as jackass presents bad grandpa action  points and many others including the  mainline jackass movies he told gq in a  2021 interview writing gave me  confidence as a person it was like i  don't have to just worry about trying to  make it i can do this and feel satisfied  and engaged luckily for fans in  knoxville alike the writer turned actor  did make it and he even turned down some  big opportunities along the way  many actors had become mega famous after  appearing on nbc's iconic sketch comedy  show saturday night live but johnny  knoxville turned down the long-running  show right around when he was shooting  the jackass pilot in a 2005 interview  with the washington times knoxville  detailed his decision saying it was at  the point where i either say yes to my  friends where we had all the control or  yes to saturday night live where none of  my friends were really going to be there  and i had no control i just thought i  made the right decision knoxville told  the hollywood reporter that his role on  snl would have consisted of him doing  solo stunts each week he told the outlet  they were going to give me like five  minutes each week to do what i do but  that would just be me and i couldn't do  both our show was about to go so i kind  of bet on us as opposed to on myself i  wasn't going to have complete control  like we did on jackass it was  a smart move in 2005 knoxville hosted  snl proving that with a little patience  you can have your cake and eat it too  johnny knoxville might live a wild and  crazy lifestyle on the screen but  off-screen he's a family man he's a  father of three and has been married  twice knoxville and his ex-wife melanie  cates had a daughter named madison now  an adult who lives in austin as of 2021  yet the two have since divorced and  knoxville is now married to naomi nelson  the couple had two children together  rocco and arlo to no one's surprise  knoxville doesn't want his kids to  follow in his stunt performing footsteps  he told access in a 2010 interview  pranks are fine no stunts i don't want  rocco or madison doing any stunts as  you'd expect his parenting techniques  are far different than his acting  methods as gq noted in a 2021 interview  quote knoxville is notably attentive to  the physical safety of his children  johnny knoxville has endured his fair  share of injuries over the years while  shooting jackass but there's one  incident that really stands out in 2007  knoxville tours urethra during a  motorcycle stunt gone wrong while  shooting jackass presents matt hoffman's  tribute to evel knievel when i came off  the ramp i let go the bike he goes 20  feet in the air and comes down and  breaks its handlebars off in my crotch  so  yeah knoxville said in a 2021 gq  interview i wasn't even supposed to do  anything i think i just showed up that  day and someone kind of threw out that i  should try and backflip a motorcycle i'm  like oh yeah i got that the result the  crash led to knoxville having to  self-administer a catheter for the next  three years but he took it all in stride  telling gq at the time i was like i  can't wait to tell the story everybody  loves a good story  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  jackass are coming soon subscribe to our  youtube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one
 

